**Outcomes and seal validation.** Store one four-byte record per logical tuple: `repr(C) { status: u8, target: u8, reason: u16 }`, with no implicit padding. Status codes 0 through 6 are NotRequested, Pending, Filled, Invalid, Undecided, Refused and reserved Missing, respectively; the first-slice publisher rejects Missing. Target codes 0 through 5 are none, original L, original C, P, tau and reciprocal/omega, respectively. The logical array index supplies the original tuple; the seal supplies selected original positions. Reason zero means no obstruction, one means strictly negative and two means no strict positive separation. For Refused, codes `0x0101..0x0104` encode DomainReason in the explicit order NonpositiveInput, ZeroInDivisor, NegativeRoot, UnboundedImage. Codes `0x0201..0x0205` encode ArithmeticFailure in the explicit order NonFinite, InvertedEndpoints, ZeroInDivisor, NegativeRoot, Overflow; `0x0301` encodes AccuracyFailure::InvalidBound; `0x0401..0x0405` preserve the same five scalar causes nested inside AccuracyFailure::Arithmetic. Target P identifies Product, tau identifies SquareRoot, and reciprocal/omega identifies Reciprocal, preserving the operation as well as cause. NotRequested, Pending and Filled require target none and reason zero. Invalid requires target L/C and reason one; Undecided requires target L/C/P/tau and reason two. Refused requires the target-specific cause set below; a numeric code alone never authorizes a different operation. All other status/target/reason combinations refuse validation. Literal, length, environment, policy and resource errors are phase failures; arithmetic-environment admission precedes traversal. This is a closed version-one vocabulary, not the Rust enum discriminant encoding. Contract, coverage and resource errors are phase refusals, not numerical cell outcomes. No unknown kernel error may be truncated into sixteen bits: the exhaustive encoding test must either prove a lossless supported mapping or force a revised decision before implementation. No diagnostic strings or variable-size per-cell errors are retained.

The closed Refused mapping is as follows. Common codes `0x0201`, `0x0202`, `0x0205`, `0x0301`, `0x0401`, `0x0402` and `0x0405` retain NonFinite, InvertedEndpoints, Overflow, InvalidBound and their listed accuracy-wrapped forms at the consuming kernel stage. In particular, an InvalidBound raised inside root or reciprocal while checking its predecessor radius belongs to root or reciprocal respectively; it is not reassigned to the predecessor because the consuming stage's guard refused while the predecessor's operation completed. P additionally admits only `0x0104`, from `KernelError::BinaryDomain { function: Product, entry: cell, reason: UnboundedImage }`. Tau additionally admits `0x0103`, `0x0104`, `0x0204` and `0x0404`; its Domain errors must name SquareRoot and the original cell. Reciprocal/omega additionally admits `0x0102`, `0x0104`, `0x0203` and `0x0403`; its Domain errors must name Reciprocal and the original cell. Code `0x0101` is reserved and invalid in this version. P with NegativeRoot or ZeroInDivisor, tau with ZeroInDivisor, and reciprocal with NegativeRoot therefore refuse validation. The target supplies the function only after checking the original error's function and entry. Common malformed-input/bracket causes and guarded root/divisor causes are defensive encodings; their presence in the table is not a claim of reachable failure after valid input/barrier admission. Bare Overflow (`0x0205`) and accuracy-wrapped Overflow (`0x0405`) are defensive encodings: both numerical kernels remap bare arithmetic overflow to UnboundedImage, and displacement calculation returns ArithmeticFailure rather than AccuracyFailure. The other accuracy-wrapped `0x04xx` codes are likewise defensive in this chain. Reachable finite-image cases and defensive injections are tested separately.

Every `LcProductError::Loan`, `KernelError::Quantity`, `KernelError::Contract` and `KernelError::CoverageMismatch` is a phase failure, preserving its original structured error outside the four-byte cell record and making an already-started candidate cancel-only. `KernelError::BinaryDomain` is a cell refusal only for the exact Product/UnboundedImage case above; every other function/reason/entry combination is a phase failure. `KernelError::Domain`, `Arithmetic` and `Accuracy` map to a cell refusal only through the listed matching target/cause cases; every unlisted variant, nested cause or mismatched entry/function is a phase failure. This includes resource, literal, length, environment and policy failures. `Invalid(Product)` is type-valid through `classify` but mathematically unreachable after valid positive L/C enclosures and a sound Product; treat it as a defensive cancel-only phase failure, not an Invalid cell code. The same rule rejects any other unsupported Invalid target, including Root. Undecided supports exactly L/C/P/tau; Ready must contain the requested omega and its required dependencies or fail the phase. Exhaustive tests must cover these type-valid defensive cases without presenting them as reachable numerical examples.

