Pin real N/N−1 boundaries with prior usage on the original immutable account for original and one-cell invocation, application slot/work/scratch limits, metadata constructors, admission prefixes, complete traversal, repeated publication, readers, cleanup and residence. Include invocation-dominant and output-dominant shapes and zero capacity. Independently reconstruct X, all unchanged shared layouts, 18 debits, 21 identities, actual vacancy reuse, slab/word boundaries, exact growth and spare-capacity B/S values, aggregate elements and terminal revision headroom. Setup must fit the same fixed ceiling; an earlier setup refusal does not test application admission. Isolate the identical internal 64-byte publication-shell plan if dominated in the public lifecycle. Require refusal before any output or side allocation for malformed contracts and failed preflight, and preserve acquired-prefix cleanup for later allocation injection.

