## Floor clamp against a rational wall · `sec:nrz:matrix-loans-clamp-floor`

**Decision (Floor-clamp value member)** · `dec:nrz:matrix-loans-clamp-floor-value`

Specify the value law max(s,a) as a closed binary64 member with entry point `Heap::request_pointwise_clamp_floor`. This decision fixes its contract, not executable support. Follow the single planner, traversal, three-reading publication and lifetime mechanism of (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-kernel-family-contract`), (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-kernel-family-shared`). The profile has a varying host-origin input s and a host-origin per-tile scalar wall operand under (`dec:nrz:matrix-loans-clamp-floor-wall`), with `RepresentedInputs` coverage on both operands and the result. The varying input and result have equal C by k extents, k positive and identity cell/component incidence; the wall has one cell and one component, read at (0,0) for every target. The wall is the right operand only; preserve original operand order and the varying input's demand layout. Refuse a swapped pin/operand pair as `WrongLoan` and an original operation with a left-side wall as `UnsupportedContract`; refuse a wall that is not one cell and one component as `UnsupportedBinaryExtent`. Admit center-only, center/total and center/total/error host forms; missing total denotes zero, and every declared role gates filled coverage, including error already included in total. Require fresh destination total/error targets, full-shape structural-zero exclusion in both scopes on both inputs and output, and the common shape, axis and attachment checks. The exact rational wall is an operand of the original checked operation, not an independently caller-selected numerical coefficient. The descriptor and original-identity obligations are (`rule:nrz:descriptor-binding-clamp-floor`). Scalar owns the finite selection/enclosure law; matrix owns both source pins, demand, companions and publication. No new request structure or original-operation constructor is selected here.

The clamp entry point refuses every other member's recipe, including Square, reciprocal, square root, retained prepared expm1, Product, Quotient and projected forms; every other entry point refuses clamp. Retain `UnsupportedContract` for an unsupported form or expected-member/captured-kind mismatch and `WrongLoan` for substituted one-cell law or immutable-seal pairing, with typed structural, layout, coverage, stale/foreign and resource refusals. Admission refusal returns the identical request and both pins with its performed Work prefix. Binary32, precision conversion, gathers, nonlocal/statistical companions and arbitrary expression substitution remain unsupported. Neither application-origin operand is admitted by this profile; the clamp is neither a chained consumer nor an admitted producer under (`dec:nrz:matrix-loans-chained-applications`).

**Rule (Floor-clamp images and three readings)** · `rule:nrz:matrix-loans-clamp-floor-readings`

The represented input is a finite binary64 center x and nonnegative finite total r, denoting the exact dyadic set [x-r,x+r]; its mathematical ends need not be binary64 values. Build the temporary outward box S=[l,u] by the existing nonlinear member construction: l is the lower endpoint of `singleton(x).sub(singleton(r))` and u the upper endpoint of `singleton(x).add(singleton(r))`, written x ⊖ r and x ⊕ r. Keep that construction at zero radius: it can widen or fail at a format limit even then, under (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-binary-numerics`). Stored endpoint conversion is not implied. With a zero-total wall c=a the whole image is [max(l,a),max(u,a)], the center is ŷ=max(x,a), and numerical error e is zero. The total R is the outward displacement of the whole image from ŷ. Selecting the maximum of two finite represented values introduces no rounding; this assertion covers neither input-box construction nor displacement arithmetic or companion conversion.

For an enclosed rational wall, let its finite binary64 center c and nonnegative finite total t denote the exact dyadic wall box A=[c-t,c+t], with a in A. Admission requires c=RN(a), nearest with ties to even; the candidate is ŷ=max(x,c)=max(x,RN(a)). The whole image is W=[max(l,c-t),max(u,c+t)], enclosed outward for displacement arithmetic. The nominal error at represented centers is zero because selection is exact. Set e=t: the already outward wall total is itself representable, so no additional rounding is needed and zero is preserved when t=0. This wall-representation error is additional to the nominal reading of (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-binary-numerics`). Indeed max is 1-Lipschitz in its wall, so abs(max(x,b)-max(x,c)) <= abs(b-c) <= t for every b in A. Set R=max(e, outward displacement of W from ŷ). A zero ŷ is stored as canonical +0. The successful stored readings are finite ŷ, R and e with 0 <= e <= R; for every v in the exact input set and every fixed b in A, abs(max(v,b)-ŷ) <= R, and abs(max(x,b)-ŷ) <= e. Thus the error a reader receives covers the rational wall's representation width; that width is not a second uncertain physical source. This Cartesian enclosure makes no independence claim. Store only center, total and error, with exact dyadic result set [ŷ-R,ŷ+R], no Lower/Upper slabs and no stored-endpoint reading. Incoming error of s participates once through r; the wall's declared error is already included in t and is not added again. The target is exact containment, with no absolute/relative tolerance or accuracy search, under (`thm:nrz:descriptor-binding-kernel-enclosure`). Malformed/nonfinite inputs or inability to form finite outward readings refuse; finite signed inputs, canonical zero and subnormals receive no artificial positive-domain restriction. Preserve typed contract, resource and numerical-refusal distinctions and the original cell/component location.

**Decision (Per-tile scalar wall carrier)** · `dec:nrz:matrix-loans-clamp-floor-wall`

Carry the declared rational wall a as the right per-tile scalar operand of the original checked clamp operation, in an ordinary pinned host bundle. Admission performs a charged correspondence check after authenticating every declared wall role as filled at (0,0), and before any allocation. An unfilled wall refuses at admission, including a hole in its declared error role; no unchecked wall reaches evaluation. Read the authenticated wall center and its total, or zero for an absent total, and compare them exactly with the original rational operand; the declared error role is authenticated and not compared. This is the member's correspondence and representation check under (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-kernel-family-shared`), not a numerical domain check. It neither scans the varying input nor speculates about a cell's numerical success under (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-binary-numerics`); domain checks remain in selected evaluation. Authentication, filled-role inspection, wall loads and exact comparisons all carry their performed Work prefix, including on refusal; the code slice owes the exact tariff.

Require c=RN(a), nearest with ties to even, and `t=t*`, the least binary64 at or above abs(RN(a)-a), zero exactly when a is representable. Interpret c and t as exact dyadics: check t>=abs(c-a) and, when t>0, pred(t)<abs(c-a), where pred(t) is the immediately preceding binary64 value. No rounded subtraction or rounded endpoint comparison may stand in for these checks. Zero representations are canonical +0; in particular a=0 requires canonical +0 bits for both c and t. Refuse a different center as `ClampWallCenterMismatch`, even if its box encloses a, including a wall whose nearest binary64 is not finite because the center must be finite; refuse failed enclosure as `ClampWallNotEnclosed`; refuse an enclosing total that is not the least canonical total as `ClampWallTotalMismatch`. These three named reasons are admission refusals on the request, returning the identical request and both pins with the performed Work prefix, not cell outcomes. Their implementation remains owed. A free total would again be a caller-chosen numerical coefficient: two clamps of the same input at the same rational wall could publish different bytes and refuse differently downstream. Since e=t is uniform, inflating t would load every cell with error and admit the excluded uncertain wall indirectly. Retain the checked association with the original rational operand and the immutable bundle identity through evaluation, publication and historical reading; equal bytes or an independently valid wall cannot replace that association.

The lowering target is the hoisted prelude region in (`rule:nrz:descriptor-binding-hoisted-constants`). Once a hoisted prelude region is admitted as a one-cell binary operand under (`rule:nrz:descriptor-binding-exact-constant-outstanding`), the wall moves to that lowering and only its origin changes: the member, law, admission checks and readings remain unchanged. Its lifetime follows (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-prelude-key`), and graph flush remains with (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-boundary`). The future prelude producer must publish exactly the admitted wall representation; a target-bounded export of the kind specified for β in (`rule:nrz:descriptor-binding-exact-constant-region`) does not qualify. Chained operands remain under (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-chain-outstanding`). No recipe-carried pair is introduced. `Elementwise` has no parameter fields, and `CellContract` retains input extents, output extent, member kind and invocation allowance, not a wall. Coefficient/program constructors and a larger universal seal remain excluded by (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-kernel-family-contract`), (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-kernel-family-resources`). The wall uses the binary two-pin incidence and lifetime model; the code slice owes its closed original correspondence, exact admission Work, complete resource inventory, independent ABI/byte pins and cleanup evidence. No other member's allowance or pin is assigned to clamp by analogy.

**Requirement (Floor-clamp value evidence still owed)** · `req:nrz:matrix-loans-clamp-floor-controls`

The scalar code slice must prove selection, outward displacement and canonical-zero behavior independently, including the control that R=0 when the whole outward input box lies below a zero-total exactly represented wall. For a non-singleton wall enclosure the image can still have wall width there; do not erase that numerical error. Include both strict sides, touching, crossing, singleton equality, zero-radius outward widening, neighboring floats, signed zero, subnormals, finite-range refusal and a non-dyadic rational wall such as 1/10. Exact CAS clamp evidence and an independent integer/rational oracle decoding the represented values must check full image and nominal containment, not rounded ŷ minus/plus R as an oracle. The exact branch premise is (`alg:nrz:enclosures-design-clamp`). The later engine slice owes rejection of a non-nearest enclosing wall center and a nearest center with inadequate total, an over-wide total that still encloses a, noncanonical zero wall representations, an unfilled declared wall role at admission, original operand/wall substitutions, complete masks, continuation after local refusal, atomic publication, resource boundaries and every ownership state, plus cross-member substitution for every ordered pair of distinct admitted members under (`req:nrz:matrix-loans-kernel-family-controls`), (`req:nrz:matrix-loans-binary-controls`). Neither this contract nor unchanged family tests discharge those controls.

**Rule (Floor-clamp value boundary and later decisions)** · `rule:nrz:matrix-loans-clamp-floor-outstanding`

The scalar max primitive belongs to the later scalar slice; the checked member, its invocation tariff, original correspondence constructor, literal resource inventories and full family controls belong to the later engine slice. This value slice does not specify the later slope member's separate entry point or three-role representation, extend the single-valued kernel enclosure theorem to a set-valued law, or admit derivative composition. That theorem extension is a separate prerequisite for the slope contract. The deterministic full-box argument in (`rule:nrz:matrix-core-jacobian-contract`) includes verified derivative error and remainder or a direct enclosure; its nonlinear covariance statement is separately only the covariance of a linearization. Neither is replaced by, or inferred from, a generalized slope at the clamp kink. An uncertain wall, including a wall given by a declared region under (`alg:nrz:enclosures-design-clamp`), is excluded: the wall box here encloses one declared exact rational, not uncertain wall data. Binary32, general g(max(s,a)), derivatives with respect to the wall, covariance propagation, standalone prepared owners and a network gain/uniqueness certificate remain outside this value slice. Golden schema work, measurement and implementation status are not supplied by these statements.

## Retained dyadic powers · `sec:nrz:matrix-loans-dyadic-power`

**Decision (Retained dyadic-power member)** · `dec:nrz:matrix-loans-dyadic-power-member`

`RetainedDyadicPower` implements the retained CAS-prepared owner; `Heap::request_pointwise_dyadic_power` remains its specified closed member entry point. Retained preparation is supplied, while masked application remains outstanding. Follow the expm1 retained-owner route of (`dec:nrz:matrix-loans-prepared-owner`), with preparation through bindings, the actual returned checked authority and its producing CAS privately paired and frozen for every retained use. Preparation calls the existing `Cas::enclose` through bindings on the original power request and context, with the ordered coordinate box reconstructed exactly from the represented admitted domain; it retains the returned `CheckedEnclosure`, including its request, certificate and checked interval, with the producing CAS. This selects the existing positive-power enclosure judgment rather than a new preparation service because it already proves inclusion over that whole domain; it does not certify native rounding. A bounded width refinement is preparation policy, not an accuracy target for the native member, and a completed checked enclosure need not meet that width goal to supply inclusion authority. Individually funded uses retain that same immutable owner under (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-prepared-owner-retention`), (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-prepared-owner-release`); equal coefficients or keys do not authenticate another owner. No supplied authority, coefficient constructor, mutable graph adapter or matrix-side slice producer is admitted. CAS owns exact evidence, bindings original meaning, scalar the native schedule and matrix preparation, retention and publication under (`dec:nrz:transcendental-scalar-owner`). The native proof bridge is (`dec:nrz:transcendental-dyadic-power-bridge`).

The exponent comes only from the original checked power operation, and admission compares its exact value with the prepared authority and schedule before allocation. There is no caller exponent field or parameter added to the element law; parameter correspondence is an original-operation obligation as in (`dec:nrz:matrix-loans-clamp-floor-wall`). Preserve original context, operand identity, source and result bindings, represented domain and captured owner/use correspondence under (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-kernel-family-contract`). Inputs arrive as heap-bound checked declarations under (`prin:nrz:descriptor-binding-float-heap`). Bind the enclosure judgment's original request, exact domain, checked endpoints and proof/checker revision together with the scalar native-argument revision, exact exponent and FMA-or-separate-steps choice in the prepared authority key and the owner's seal; this composition leaves the CAS judgment and its meaning unchanged. Include that same scalar revision, exponent and instruction choice in the lowering key under (`rule:nrz:transcendental-keys`); the arithmetic model fixes contraction and permitted target instructions under (`req:nrz:transcendental-schedule-proof`), (`req:nrz:transcendental-small-schedule`).

Select binary64 center-only host points with `RepresentedInputs`, equal C by k input/output extents with k positive and identity component incidence, following (`dec:nrz:matrix-loans-prepared-expm1-slice`). A selected center x denotes [x,x], within the retained admitted domain. The domain, exact-one result after validation, outward-only target and closed numerical refusals are (`def:nrz:transcendental-power-operation`), (`def:nrz:transcendental-power-domain`), (`req:nrz:transcendental-power-target`), (`rule:nrz:transcendental-refusals`). Native domain checks occur during selected evaluation under (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-kernel-family-shared`). Store ordered binary64 Lower/Upper endpoints and separate center, total and numerical error by (`rule:nrz:transcendental-result-evidence`); neither endpoint slack nor a midpoint supplies the nominal error proof. A successful reading encloses the actual nominal value by its error and the whole image by its total, with error included once. No width, relative or absolute accuracy target follows from inclusion; final composition accuracy remains with (`rule:nrz:transcendental-target-budget`).

Use the shared admission, demand, traversal, publication, refusal association and lifetime mechanism of (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-kernel-family-shared`), with fresh destination companions and the member's own complete profile. Each existing entry point refuses this member and its entry point refuses the other members; (`req:nrz:matrix-loans-kernel-family-controls`) also excludes substituting the q=1/2 power for square root or the reverse. Center/total box conversion to input endpoints remains a separate contract shared with expm1 under (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-prepared-expm1-outstanding`), (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-endpoint-view`). Prepared producer/consumer chaining remains open under (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-chain-outstanding`). Binary32, physical-input coverage, broader rational exponents, exponent zero, logarithm, derivative bounds and a new public construction or authentication surface are outside this member contract.

